  "semantic_scope": {
    "normalization": "For every finite Nat word w and every Nat carry e, natValue (Agent8.normalize w e) = natValue w + e, directly reusing the unchanged Agent3 digitValue_normalize theorem via definitional value equality.",
    "fiber_first_step": "Every n in numericFiber h c steps to natValue (Agent8.normalize (coefficientWord h c) 0). No extra valid-profile assumption is needed for this member implication.",
    "family": "For m >= 0 and k > 0, all 5*11^m distinct positive protectedSeeds have width 2*(m+k+1), share second value natValue(target m k), and avoid palindromes at every time 1..k+1.",
    "initial_condition": "If a particular protected seed is initially nonpalindromic, it avoids palindromes at every time 0..k+1. Safety itself does not remove the unique initial palindrome; the root-owned filter module does that.",
    "limits": [
      "The horizon parameter k may change the family; no single seed safe at every horizon is asserted.",
      "The family is the selected union of complete fixed-width profile fibers; no global count of every two-step preimage is asserted."
    ]
  },
